  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 230 AM CDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nMonday-Next Weekend:\nA quiet week of weather ahead as a ridge gradually builds east\nout of the Four Corners region, supporting a trend towards above\nnormal temperatures and persistent dry conditions. Temperatures\nare expected to reach towards the middle to upper 80s by mid to\nlate week. This is 10+ degrees above normal for early October. \nConfidence is high in this stretch of warm weather, as seen with\nsmall interquartile spreads in the NBM.\n\nThe main storyline looking ahead this week into next week will\nbe the persist dry and warm weather that may support some fire\nweather concerns. Daily minimum relative humidity values are\nprogged to be around 30-40%. The lowest values will be focused\neast of Highway 65, where NBM may be struggling to capture even\nlower values around 20-30%. Given the conditions in place,\nlocalized areas of elevated fire weather by mid to late this \nweek. However, winds do remain rather light through the week and\nshould limit the extent of fire weather concerns.\n\nIt will be important to keep an eye on the forecast into early \nnext week, as ensemble guidance continues to highlight a dry \nperiod of weather. Minimal rainfall with recent systems will \ncontinue to amplify the drought and early Fall fire weather \nconditions.",
